   "old": "has about $(120/0.1)\\times(25/0.2)=1{,}200\\times125=150{,}000$, consistent with the ≈110,000–120,000 lidar points per frame in the same dataset [E].",
   "new": "has about $(120/0.1)\\times(25/0.2)=1{,}200\\times125=150{,}000$ angular cells. That is of the same order as the ≈110,000–120,000 points per frame that the dataset's own lidar records, whose grid is not given here; directions with no return, such as the sky, also lower a lidar's point count [E].",
