   "id": "01_A3-A6_E2-E5-046",
   "finding": "report #4 (tag and currency part); report §3 flag (currency)",
   "old": "fell from RMB 500–1,000 in early 2024 to RMB 200–400 in 2025, about \\$28–56 at an assumed exchange rate of RMB 7.1 per dollar (200 ÷ 7.1 ≈ 28 and 400 ÷ 7.1 ≈ 56), as dual-chip cascades replaced quad-chip designs. The same source puts it at 1/5–1/10 of a lidar's price and expects it to fall below \\$100 [T, ResearchInChina; not independently corroborated].",
   "new": "fell from ¥500–1,000 in early 2024 to ¥200–400 in 2025, about \\$28–56 at an assumed exchange rate of ¥7.1 per dollar (200 ÷ 7.1 ≈ 28 and 400 ÷ 7.1 ≈ 56), as dual-chip cascades replaced quad-chip designs. The same source puts this radar at 1/5–1/10 of a lidar's price and expects it to fall below \\$100 [MR, ResearchInChina; not independently corroborated].",
   "why": "Chinese prices are written in ¥ (How to read) and ResearchInChina is [MR]; the \\$100 clause awaits its source."
