  {
   "id": "01_A3-A6_E2-E5-047",
   "finding": "report #28",
   "old": "It weights mAP by one half and averages it with five error measures (translation, size, orientation, velocity and attribute), each converted to a 0–1 score.",
   "new": "It is $\\text{NDS}=\\frac{1}{10}\\left[5\\,\\text{mAP}+\\sum_{k=1}^{5}\\left(1-\\min(1,\\text{mTP}_k)\\right)\\right]$, reported ×100: half the weight is on mAP (0–1 scale) and a tenth on each of five true-positive error measures $\\text{mTP}_k$ (translation, size, orientation, velocity and attribute), each turned into a 0–1 score by $1-\\min(1,\\text{mTP}_k)$.",
   "why": "'Weights by one half and averages it with' was ambiguous for the section's headline metric."
  },
  {
   "id": "01_A3-A6_E2-E5-048",
   "finding": "report §3 flag (spelling); report §1 Problem 3 (tags)",
   "old": "(≤50 m, center-distance matching; NDS = nuScenes detection score). nuScenes is a public driving dataset with camera, lidar and radar recordings; its \"test\" split is scored only by the organizers' server. Center-distance matching counts a detection as correct when its centre lies within a set ground-plane distance of the true object's centre, rather than requiring box overlap, which is more forgiving of small position errors. This is a landscape comparison across methods and publication years, not a controlled sensor ablation. The method names (RoPETR, LION, SparseLIF) are published detectors:\n- best camera-only NDS about **70.9** (RoPETR, 2025);\n- lidar-only 73.9 (LION, 2024);\n- fusion 77.0 (SparseLIF, 2024).",
   "new": "(≤50 m, centre-distance matching; NDS = nuScenes detection score). nuScenes is a public driving dataset with camera, lidar and radar recordings; its \"test\" split is scored only by the organizers' server. Centre-distance matching counts a detection as correct when its centre lies within a set ground-plane distance of the true object's centre, rather than requiring box overlap, which is more forgiving of small position errors. This is a landscape comparison across methods and publication years, not a controlled sensor ablation. The method names (RoPETR, LION, SparseLIF) are published detectors:\n- best camera-only NDS about **70.9** (RoPETR, 2025) [I];\n- lidar-only 73.9 (LION, 2024) [I];\n- fusion 77.0 (SparseLIF, 2024) [I].",
   "why": "British 'centre' as elsewhere; published benchmark results are [I] (academic papers)."
  },
  {
   "id": "01_A3-A6_E2-E5-049",
   "finding": "report #26 (wording part)",
   "old": "the camera matches: **camera error is almost purely depth**",
   "new": "the camera's AP rises to about the lidar's: **camera error is almost purely depth**",
   "why": "Says what the camera matches; the supporting values are listed as needs_source."
  },
  {
